From: Gemini Mainline Maintainers <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: mediatek: use MT6797 multipoint target addresses

The MT6797 vendor USB11 driver unconditionally switches the controller to
multipoint addressing in musbfsh_start().  Preserve that hardware contract in
the mainline MUSB data.  Without it, Linux writes the assigned device address
to MUSB_FADDR instead of the per-endpoint target-address registers at 0x480,
and control transfers fail after SET_ADDRESS.

---
 drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/mediatek.c
@@ -409,6 +409,10 @@ static const struct musb_hdrc_config mt6797_usb11_hdrc_config = {
 	.fifo_cfg = mt6797_usb11_mode_cfg,
 	.fifo_cfg_size = ARRAY_SIZE(mt6797_usb11_mode_cfg),
-	.multipoint = false,
+	/*
+	 * The vendor MT6797 USB11 start path forces is_multipoint = 1 and
+	 * therefore uses the per-endpoint target-address registers at 0x480.
+	 */
+	.multipoint = true,
 	.dyn_fifo = true,
 	.num_eps = 6,
 	.ram_bits = MTK_MUSB_RAM_BITS,
